  "result": "```js\nasync function getUser(id) {\n  const rows = await db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [id]);\n  if (!rows.length) throw new Error('Not found');\n  return rows[0];\n}\n```\n\nKey changes:\n- `async` function replaces the `callback` parameter\n- `await` replaces the callback passed to `db.query`\n- Errors propagate naturally via `throw` / rejected promise instead of `callback(err)`\n- The caller uses `try/catch` or `.catch()` instead of checking the first argument\n\nThis assumes `db.query` returns a promise. If it's still callback-based, wrap it first with `util.promisify`:\n\n```js\nconst { promisify } = require('util');\nconst dbQuery = promisify(db.query.bind(db));\n\nasync function getUser(id) {\n  const rows = await dbQuery('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [id]);\n  if (!rows.length) throw new Error('Not found');\n  return rows[0];\n}\n```",
